@TGU
Feature: the second file, given a header code of its own

  THE REMEDY, as its own tree — the sibling of `scn-tags-duplicate-code` with ONE of the
  two codes changed and nothing else. The pair is what makes the arm load-bearing: red
  then green over one header tag's difference, rather than a single assertion that could
  pass for any reason.

  Its scenario id moves with the header, because a code names the file it is written in
  — leaving `SCN-TGT-002` here would plant a SECOND fault (@SCN-STG-011's) in the tree
  whose whole job is to carry none.

  @unit @SCN-TGU-002
  Scenario: a scenario that lives in the second file
    Given the target source
